<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    [JPT] Burn It for Fuel: let its burner stockpile accept dry manure.

    THIS CURRENTLY DOES NOTHING, AND THAT IS EXPECTED. The mod on the Workshop (1823276856,
    JPT.BurnItForFuel) declares <supportedVersions>1.1, 1.2, 1.3</supportedVersions> and cannot
    load in 1.6; no continuation of it is installed. The operation is kept because it is guarded
    on the def rather than on a mod, so it costs nothing while the def is absent and starts
    working by itself the day a 1.6 continuation appears keeping the BurnItForFuel defName.

    Velcroboy's Manure used PatchOperationFindMod against the display names "[JPT] Burn It for
    Fuel" and "[JPT] Burn It for Fuel (Continued)". A continuation that renames itself - which is
    exactly what continuations do - would defeat that. Testing for the def does not care.

    Note the two-step guard: the def can exist without the storage filter having a thingDefs list
    at all, and PatchOperationAdd on a missing xpath is an error, not a no-op.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="BurnItForFuel"]/building/fixedStorageSettings/filter/thingDefs</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="BurnItForFuel"]/building/fixedStorageSettings/filter/thingDefs</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>DryManure</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
